[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit Declined"]
[Variation "Orthodox Defence, Knight Variation"]
[ECO "D37"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "transposition,solid-setup"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "3.Nf3"]
[Start "orthodox 2...e6"]

3. Nf3 { White develops the knight first and keeps the choice between Nc3 and g3 for later. } 3... Nf6 4. Bg5 ( 4. Nc3 { The Three Knights Variation, the same position as 3.Nc3 Nf6 4.Nf3. } 4... Be7 ) ( 4. e3 Be7 { No pin on f6 to worry about, so Black develops calmly. Next: castle, wait for Bd3, then ...dxc4 and ...c5. } ) ( 4. g3 Be7 5. Bg2 O-O { This is the Catalan by another move order. } ) ( 4. cxd5 exd5 5. Nc3 { The Exchange Variation with the knight on f3, the same as 3.Nc3 Nf6 4.cxd5 exd5 5.Nf3. } 5... Be7 ) 4... Be7 { The same set-up as always: bishop to e7 ends the pin, then castle. } 5. e3 ( 5. Nc3 O-O 6. e3 Nbd7 ) 5... O-O 6. Nc3 ( 6. Nbd2 Nbd7 7. Rc1 c6 ) ( 6. Qc2 Nbd7 7. Nc3 c6 ) 6... Nbd7 { The usual Queen's Gambit Declined setup, with ...c6 and ...dxc4 to come. } *
